## Corrected Solution

### Step 1: Update Your LWC Meta.xml File

Replace your `revenueDropOffTable.js-meta.xml` with:

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>62.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <masterLabel>Revenue Drop Off Table</masterLabel>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__AgentforceOutput</target>
    </targets>
    <targetConfigs>
        <targetConfig targets="lightning__AgentforceOutput">
            <sourceType name="lightning__listType" itemTypeName="c__revenueDropOffResponse"/>
        </targetConfig>
    </targetConfigs>
</LightningComponentBundle>
```

### Step 2: Update Your LWC JavaScript

Replace your `revenueDropOffTable.js` with:

```javascript
import { LightningElement, api } from 'lwc';

export default class RevenueDropOffTable extends LightningElement {
    @api value; // This will receive data from Agentforce

    columns = [
        { label: 'Customer', fieldName: 'customerName', type: 'text' },
        { label: 'Period 1', fieldName: 'period1Revenue', type: 'text' },
        { label: 'Period 2', fieldName: 'period2Revenue', type: 'text' },
        { label: 'Drop Amount', fieldName: 'dropAmount', type: 'text' },
        { label: 'Drop %', fieldName: 'dropPercentage', type: 'text' }
    ];

    get tableData() {
        if (!this.value || !Array.isArray(this.value)) {
            return [];
        }

        return this.value.map(item => ({
            customerName: item.customerName,
            period1Revenue: item.period1Revenue,
            period2Revenue: item.period2Revenue,
            dropAmount: item.dropAmount,
            dropPercentage: item.dropPercentage
        }));
    }
}
```

### Step 3: Create Custom Lightning Types

You need to create these metadata files in your project:

**Create folder:** `force-app/main/default/customMetadata/`

**File 1:** `revenueDropOffResponse.lightningType/schema.json`
```json
{
  "title": "Revenue Drop Off Response",
  "description": "Revenue Drop Off Analysis Response",
  "lightning:type": "@apexClassType/c__Customer_RevenueDropOffAction$DropOffData"
}
```

**File 2:** `revenueDropOffResponse.lightningType/renderer.json`
```json
{
    "collection": {
        "renderer": {
            "componentOverrides": {
                "$": {
                    "definition": "c/revenueDropOffTable"
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

